145 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 76 0 R/T(This design allows for a 4-bit Programmable Gain Control. By toggling these four switches, we aren't limited to just 4 gain settings; we can create 16 different gain combinations by using them in parallel. This gives the ESP32 the ability to perform 'Auto-Ranging,' choosing the best gain to keep the signal within the 12-bit ADC's optimal window.)/E(This design allows for a 4-bit Programmable Gain Control. By toggling these four switches, we aren't limited to just 4 gain settings; we can create 16 different gain combinations by using them in parallel. This gives the ESP32 the ability to perform 'Auto-Ranging,' choosing the best gain to keep the signal within the 12-bit ADC's optimal window.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

